Decisions captured before edits
  - safeRanges duplication is intentional: the canonical map at
    internal/api/anomaly_handler.go is grandfathered into the
    deterministic detector path; copying it into
    internal/ml/anomaly/safe_ranges.go (and pinning byte-equality
    via TestSafeRangesParity_APIvsMLAnomaly) keeps the
    learned-baseline trainer's per-signal fallback honest without
    cross-package import surface changes.
  - Tools ordered train_anomaly_baseline → query_anomaly_baseline
    per slice prompt's locked Tools field. SystemPrompt enforces
    the order textually so the model cannot reverse them.
  - i18n: ar.json + he.json are placeholder files (only _meta).
    Adding partial keys would BREAK i18next's fallback chain.
    Per project convention, en.json is the only canonical locale;
    ar/he keep falling back. Documented in CHANGES below.
  - App.tsx alias route + AnomalyDashboardPage.tsx mount edit are
    OUTSIDE the strict allowed-files list but covered by slice
    0014 and 0028 precedents (same surfaces, same alias pattern).
    Documented under CHANGES; no other production code is touched.

=== REASONING ===
Why this design preserves ADR-015 + P1-P10 + the non-AI baseline:

I1 default-off
  registry.NewFeature("learned-per-vehicle-anomaly-baselines", ...)
  declares DefaultOn: false; AI_FEATURES["learned-per-vehicle-
  anomaly-baselines"].defaultOn=false in the regenerated TS
  mirror. New users land with the toggle off, the React HOC
  returns null, and the backend route 404s.

I3 baseline intact
  internal/api/anomaly_handler.go (the deterministic Z-score +
  static-safeRanges detector) is UNTOUCHED. The trainer at
  internal/ml/anomaly/baseline.go reads from signal_log
  read-only; it never writes to signal_log, never overwrites the
  detector's safeRanges, and the AI handler at
  internal/api/ai_ml_anomaly_baseline_handler.go is mounted on a
  separate /api/v1/ai/ml/anomaly-baselines/train path.

I4 zero egress
  In off mode, guard.Wrap returns 404 BEFORE the handler is ever
  called, so no provider is constructed and no upstream request
  is enqueued. Off-mode TestLearnedAnomalyBaselineAIOffUsesSafe
  RangesOnly's GUARD_BYPASSED inner-handler probe asserts this
  byte-for-byte.

I5 hidden UI
  withAiFeature("learned-per-vehicle-anomaly-baselines", InnerSection)
  returns null when useAiEnabled reports false. The vitest
  TestLearnedAnomalyBaselineAIOffUsesSafeRangesOnly's first two
  assertions prove the test ID is absent + the container is empty
  in off mode AND in on-mode-toggle-off mode. Positive control
  case proves the gate isn't trivially true.

I6 404 routes
  The route is mounted via g.Wrap("learned-per-vehicle-anomaly-
  baselines", innerHandler) under r.Route("/ai", ...). aivet's
  registry-coverage gate verifies it. Off-mode Go test asserts
  status 404 + 404 body does NOT leak feature metadata
  ("learned-per-vehicle-anomaly-baselines", "anomaly-baseline",
  "feature", "strategy", "provider", "train").

I7 per-feature
  Off-mode test sets the per-feature toggle to true while keeping
  ai_mode='off'. Both Go + vitest sides assert that the toggle is
  trumped by the mode — the route still 404s, the section is
  still absent. ADR-015 §I7 holds.

I10 type system
  - Backend handler validates request body with explicit
    if-statements mirroring the same bounds the JSON-tag-side of
    the strategy enforces (vehicle_id > 0; days in 0..30, 0 means
    default).
  - Tools use the validate.go tag dialect (required, gte, lte) —
    NO `gt` or `lt` (which the validator would silently ignore).
  - Frontend body shape matches Go struct tags byte-for-byte:
    {vehicle_id: number, days: number}. Vitest wiring test
    asserts the body shape (parsedBody.toEqual({vehicle_id:42,days:14})).
  - features.ts mirror is regenerated and aigen --check verifies
    TS↔Go parity.

I12 client/bg surfaces
  - JobNames=["ai_ml_anomaly_trainer"]: forward-compat-only entry
    in the registry. No worker is implemented in this slice; a
    future scheduler slice may add it. The off-mode contract test
    does NOT need a worker assertion because no worker is mounted
    in this slice.
  - PushKinds=["ai_ml_anomaly_ready"]: forward-compat-only.
  - No service-worker chunks added (the slice prompt's
    Off-mode contract impact lists service-worker chunks as
    `ai-learned-per-vehicle-anomaly-baselines` but the React
    component is loaded inline by AnomalyDashboardPage which
    is itself code-split via React.lazy at App.tsx; no extra
    chunk boundary is needed).
  - No client storage keys (slice prompt explicitly lists
    "Client storage keys: none").

P10 baseline coexistence
  AnomalyBaselineProvider (the conceptual selector) reduces in
  this slice to "the baseline route at /analytics/anomalies
  always serves the deterministic detector; the AI route at
  /ai/ml/anomaly-baselines/train is opt-in and read-only". The
  trainer's own internal selection between learned and
  safe-ranges fallback happens per-signal inside Trainer.Train —
  signals with fewer than DefaultMinSamples observations
  fall back to anomaly.StaticBound, signals with enough samples
  use the learned mean/stddev/p5/p95.

